KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* pointer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* more specialized: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Partial ordering of the two partial specializations is not decided by
deduction ([temp.spec.partial.order]/1).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program (-std=c++11), and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
